vendor/flame/flame_head.bin.wasm
  Derived from FLAME 2023 Open, Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems
  (https://flame.is.tue.mpg.de), licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/; model licence:
  https://flame.is.tue.mpg.de/modellicense.html).
  FLAME: T. Li, T. Bolkart, M. J. Black, H. Li and J. Romero, "Learning a model of facial shape
  and expression from 4D scans", ACM Transactions on Graphics (Proc. SIGGRAPH Asia), 2017.
  Changes made: only the head template, triangles and the first 50 identity shape components are
  kept (no expression, pose or joint data); axes are turned and metres converted to millimetres;
  the components are quantised to 16 bits. Made with tools/convert-flame.py. The .wasm suffix
  makes every static host serve the file; it is not WebAssembly. Used only by the built-in head
  scan. The FLAME licence doesn't permit pornographic use or creating fake, defamatory or
  misleading content with the model.

src/deer-skull.js
  Derived from "White-tailed Deer: Skull and Mandible" (Odocoileus virginianus), a 3D scan by the
  Smithsonian Institution, National Museum of Natural History, Department of Paleobiology (USNM PAL),
  released under Creative Commons Zero (CC0 1.0; https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).
  Source: https://3d-api.si.edu/content/document/3d_package:fcc69841-d8be-4103-be0f-143e374c9ce6/resources/USNM_PAL_Deer_skull-100k-2048-obj_std.zip
  (ark:/65665/3c5df1823-689c-44bd-8ca5-4c748c234ea2). Changes made: the skull only (no mandible),
  made symmetric about its midline, and stored as a signed distance grid of its upper half (1.5 mm
  cells, 8 bits). Made with tools/convert-skull.js. Used to carve the skull cap.

